## Component Philosophy — Dumb Components

Components are for **layout**, not logic. They receive props, lay out elements, and render.

**IN a component file:** props destructuring, `useTranslation()`, CSS class application, local UI state only (`isOpen`, `isHovered`), calling utility functions for display formatting.

**NOT in a component file:** business logic, calculations, data transformations, data fetching, anything that can be unit tested independently.

```typescript
// GOOD — logic extracted to utils
import { calcProgress, isOverdue, formatDuration } from '@utils';

export function TaskCard({ task }: TaskCardProps) {
  const { t } = useTranslation('tasks');
  return (
    <div className={styles.root}>
      <Typography variant="body-md">{task.title}</Typography>
      <Progress value={calcProgress(task.actualMinutes, task.estimatedMinutes)} />
      {isOverdue(task) && <Badge variant="error">{t('taskCard.overdue')}</Badge>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Zustand for global state, useState for local UI state

```typescript
// Global state (theme, sidebar, timer)
export const useThemeStore = create<ThemeState>(set => ({
  theme: 'dark',
  toggleTheme: () => set(state => ({ theme: state.theme === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark' })),
}));

// Local state stays in component — only for UI concerns
const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
```

