## CSS — Variables, Modules, Nesting

### No raw values — ever

Every spacing, color, font size, radius, shadow, and transition references a CSS variable from `global.css`. Use `calc()` for derived values:

```css
padding: var(--spacing-md);
margin: calc(var(--spacing-lg) + var(--spacing-xs));
```

### Spacing — T-Shirt Sizing (default: 12px)

```
--spacing-xxs: 2px    --spacing-xs: 4px     --spacing-sm: 8px
--spacing-md: 12px    --spacing-lg: 16px    --spacing-xl: 24px
--spacing-xxl: 32px   --spacing-3xl: 48px   --spacing-4xl: 64px
```

### Component-Specific Variables — Semantic Naming

Pattern: `--components-{component}-{variant}-{property}-{state}`

```css
--components-buttons-primary-bg: #3ede6f;
--components-buttons-primary-bg-hover: #6df79a;
--components-buttons-primary-bg-pressed: #9effba;
--components-buttons-primary-bg-disabled: #2e3035;
--components-buttons-primary-text: #0e0f10;
--components-buttons-primary-text-disabled: #686b74;
```

When building a component and encountering brand-specific or stateful styling, break it out into a variable following this convention.

### CSS Nesting with `&`

```css
.primary {
  background-color: var(--components-buttons-primary-bg);
  color: var(--components-buttons-primary-text);

  &:hover {
    background-color: var(--components-buttons-primary-bg-hover);
  }

  &:active {
    background-color: var(--components-buttons-primary-bg-pressed);
  }

  &:disabled {
    background-color: var(--components-buttons-primary-bg-disabled);
    color: var(--components-buttons-primary-text-disabled);
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
}
```

**Nesting rules:**
- `&` for pseudo-classes, pseudo-elements, compound selectors
- Nest `@media` inside selectors for co-located responsive styles
- Max 2 levels deep — restructure if deeper

### Responsive — Mobile First

Default CSS targets small screens. Scale up with `min-width`:
```css
.root {
  padding: var(--spacing-sm);

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
  }
}
```

