## Typography — Semantic Variants

ALL visible text goes through `<Typography>`. No raw `<p>`, `<h1>`, `<span>`.

```typescript
<Typography as="h1" variant="heading-xl" weight="bold">{t('title')}</Typography>
<Typography as="p" variant="body-md">{t('description')}</Typography>
<Typography as="span" variant="caption-sm" color="muted">{t('timestamp')}</Typography>
<Typography as="span" variant="eyebrow-md">{t('category')}</Typography>
<Typography as="span" variant="stat-lg" weight="extra">{formattedTime}</Typography>
<Typography as="label" variant="label-md">{t('fieldLabel')}</Typography>
```

### Variant categories
| Category | Use case | Sizes | Default weight |
|----------|----------|-------|----------------|
| `heading` | Page titles, section headers | xs, sm, md, lg, xl | bold |
| `subtitle` | Secondary section headers | sm, md, lg | semi |
| `body` | Paragraphs, descriptions | xs, sm, md, lg | reg |
| `label` | Form labels, nav items, buttons | xs, sm, md, lg | med |
| `caption` | Helper text, timestamps, metadata | sm, md | reg |
| `eyebrow` | Category labels, pre-headings (ALL CAPS) | sm, md, lg | semi |
| `overline` | Small caps above headings, tabs | sm, md | med |
| `code` | Inline code, monospaced data | sm, md, lg | reg |
| `stat` | Dashboard metrics, timer readouts | sm, md, lg, xl | bold |

### Weight prop overrides
`thin` (100), `light` (300), `reg` (400), `med` (500), `semi` (600), `bold` (700), `extra` (800)

